# Copy to .env for local development. Never commit the real file (already gitignored).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ vars are inlined at build/bundle time by Expo/Metro.
#
# Note: on an Android emulator, "localhost" refers to the emulator itself, not your host
# machine — use http://10.0.2.2:3000/api/v1 there. On iOS simulator or a browser (expo start
# --web), localhost works directly. On a physical device, use your machine's LAN IP.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL="http://localhost:3000/api/v1"

# Google Sign-In (major-upgrade phase). Public by design (an OAuth client ID, not a secret).
# WEB_CLIENT_ID is required even on Android — expo-auth-session's Google provider uses it as the
# token audience; ANDROID_CLIENT_ID additionally needs the app's package name + release SHA-1/256
# fingerprint registered in Google Cloud Console before a real (non-Expo-Go) build can complete
# sign-in. Without these set, the "Continue with Google" button stays inert; phone-OTP sign-in
# works either way. See ARCHITECTURE.md for the exact manual Google Cloud Console steps.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=""
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=""
